# What is tracked here is what was *authored*: code, experiment declarations,
# documentation, and the metrics that constitute the findings. Everything else
# is regenerable from those, and most of it is large enough that committing it
# would make the repository unusable.
#
# The rule, stated once: if a script can produce it, it does not belong in git.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source corpora — 7.4 GB, 29 folders, redistributed from upstream datasets.
# raw-data/README.md and MANIFEST.md record provenance so the tree can be
# reassembled; the bytes themselves are not ours to version.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
raw-data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The prior study's derived artefacts (199 MB). Its own scripts regenerate
# these, and model/data/ already holds the copies this workspace reads.
# Its tools/, docs/ and pre-registration ARE tracked — they are load-bearing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
prior-study/data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trained weight matrices, wherever they appear.
#
# Deliberately narrower than excluding results/runs/ wholesale: manifest.json
# and metrics.json stay tracked, so the leaderboard is versioned and a number
# can be traced to the commit that produced it. Only the blobs are dropped.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.npy
*.npz
*.parquet
*.pt
*.bin
*.safetensors

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The site's data bundle, re-admitted against the rule above.
#
# The rule is "if a script can produce it, it does not belong in git", and
# scripts/export_site.py does produce all of this. But it produces it *from*
# the weight blobs excluded above, which means a CI runner with a fresh clone
# cannot regenerate it, and a deploy that cannot rebuild its own inputs is not
# reproducible in any useful sense.
#
# So the bundle is tracked. It is roughly 10 MB, and almost all of it is two
# things the browser cannot do without: the nearest-neighbour tables (5.5 MB
# across ids and scores) and the EASE item-item matrix (1.2 MB, shipped as the
# 366 rows the demo can actually index rather than all 1,790). The measurements
# read from metrics.json are under 200 KB of it.
#
# Same reasoning as keeping metrics.json above — the artefact is small, it is
# the published claim, and versioning it is what lets any figure on the site
# be traced to a commit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!site/public/data/
!site/public/data/*.bin

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Azure — holds the subscription id. Not secret, but per-developer.
model/cloud/config.json
.env

# macOS
.DS_Store
